      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c2a35b85-3f4a-51fa-bd77-395778bde063",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Piet Norval, Emilio Sánchez, Wayne Ferreira, Kevin Ullyett, Slobodan Živojinović, Goran Ivanišević, Balázs Taróczy\n- Events: 1988 Olympic Games, 1990 Belgian Indoor Championships – Doubles, 1992 Summer Olympics, 2000 Stockholm Open – Doubles\n- Roles: player, captain, tournament director\n- Topics: doubles tennis, wheelchair tennis\n\nFacts:\n- Emilio Sánchez won the men's doubles silver medal at the 1988 Olympic Games.\n- Emilio Sánchez and Slobodan Živojinović won the 1990 Belgian Indoor Championships doubles title by defeating Goran Ivanišević and Balázs Taróczy 7–5, 6–3 in the final.\n- The two previous champions of the 1990 Belgian Indoor Championships doubles event did not participate in 1990.\n- Piet Norval represented South Africa in the doubles competition at the 1992 Summer Olympics in Barcelona with partner Wayne Ferreira.\n- Piet Norval and Kevin Ullyett were the defending champions at the 2000 Stockholm Open doubles event, but they lost in the semifinals.\n- Emilio Sánchez captained Spain to Davis Cup success in 2008.\n- In 2012, Emilio Sánchez was a tournament director for two wheelchair tennis events.\n- Emilio Sánchez won three Grand Slam doubles titles.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d50fcaae-da3f-5fb7-9f40-c0e8c4fb6cdc",
        "text": "Page: Piet Norval. Sentence: The right-hander represented his native country in the doubles competition at the 1992 Summer Olympics in Barcelona, where he partnered Wayne Ferreira.\nPage: Emilio Sánchez. Sentence: He won three Grand Slam doubles titles and the men's doubles silver medal at the 1988 Olympic Games.\nPage: Emilio Sánchez. Sentence: Sanchez since retiring captained his nation to Davis Cup success in 2008.\nPage: Emilio Sánchez. Sentence: In 2012 Sanchez was a tournament director for two wheelchair tennis events.\nPage: 2000 Stockholm Open – Doubles. Sentence: Piet Norval and Kevin Ullyett were the defending champions, but lost in the semifinals this year.\nPage: 1990 Belgian Indoor Championships – Doubles. Sentence: Neither of them participated in 1990.\nPage: 1990 Belgian Indoor Championships – Doubles. Sentence: Emilio Sánchez and Slobodan Živojinović won the title, defeating Goran Ivanišević and Balázs Taróczy 7–5, 6–3, in the final.",
